// ( ) empty tuple and ( a, b, ... ) / ( a, ) tuples are accepted and reported as
// not implemented; a single parenthesized expression ( a ) is plain grouping.
// () is the empty tuple; ( a ) is plain grouping; ( a, b ) / ( a, ) is a TUPLE.
// A tuple is modelled as a plain list - the value model has one sequence type - so
